; mold: which aircraft flies which leg, found by flying the day and, at
; each leg, asking a network of actors that grows as it's needed, like a
; slime mold, which aircraft still can. An experiment in three layers:
; a simulation that flies a schedule; over it, constraints as actors
; sending each other messages, as a CP-SAT solver propagates; and over
; them a search that ticks the simulation and goes on, stops or branches.
; And what the actors cost beside the same thing as a value and a loop.
;
;     node bin/slightc.ts --target x86_64 -o mold examples/mold.slight
;     SLIGHT_CLOCK=virtual ./mold              (reads examples/mold-day.sexp)
;     SLIGHT_CLOCK=virtual ./mold day.sexp
;     ./mold --fly examples/mold-oc.ssim       (the simulation alone: the day
;                                              flown as its schedule plans it)
;     ./mold --values day.sexp                 (the mold as a value: no actors)
;     SLIGHT_CLOCK=virtual ./mold --split 2 day.sexp
;                                              (the first two choices each a
;                                              process, the islands shared out
;                                              among them)
;     ./mold --settle system day.sexp          (ask :system whether the mold is
;                                              quiet, in place of the clock)
;     ./mold --best ...                        (only the cheapest: a branch
;                                              that can't beat the best known
;                                              is left)
;     ./mold --first ...                       (only a day that flies: the
;                                              search stops at the first)
;     ./mold --slack 10 day.ssim               (an SSIM day's aircraft may fly
;                                              what their lines plan and 10 per
;                                              cent more, and no further)
;     ./mold --check minutes ...               (an aircraft's minutes are the
;                                              simulation's to check as it
;                                              flies, and no rule of the mold)
;     ./mold --stats ...                       (and what the search did)
; args: --split 2
;
; bench/mold.py runs it with sets of these, and times them, and
; t/models/mold.py makes days, and counts their assignments another way:
; examples/mold.expected is its, and t/392 to t/399's, which run the
; other ways of keeping the mold, --best, and the SSIM day.
;
; The day: aircraft, each with its type, where it starts, the minutes it
; may fly before maintenance and what a minute of it costs; and legs,
; each of a type, from an airport to another, leaving and landing at a
; minute. Every leg wants an aircraft of its type. An aircraft flies its
; legs in order, each from where the last landed, no sooner than its
; type's turn after it, and their minutes within its own. A day is a
; .sexp file (examples/mold-day.sexp, made up, of one type), or an SSIM
; file, a schedule as airlines exchange them (examples/mold-oc.ssim: a
; made-up airline's February day, 324 legs through Pittsburgh and
; Greensboro, by someone who makes schedules), which
; examples/mold-ssim.slight reads, and says what it makes of.
;
; 1. The simulation (fly). The airline as the day goes: the leg that
;    leaves next, and for each aircraft where it is, when it landed, the
;    minutes and legs it has flown, and the leg it flew last. A tick is
;    a leg leaving, in the order they leave: the simulation is told the
;    aircraft, and either flies the leg, the aircraft's place, time and
;    minutes moving on, or stops, saying why: the aircraft isn't there,
;    hasn't had its turn, is the wrong type, has flown on since, or would
;    pass its minutes. It knows nothing of what's to come. --fly is this
;    layer alone: an SSIM day flown as its own lines plan it, which
;    either gets to the end of the day or doesn't.
;
; 2. The mold. The model is the one tail assignment is usually given: a
;    leg doesn't choose an aircraft but its predecessor, the leg its
;    aircraft flew before it, or an aircraft's start. Where and when a
;    leg leaves, and its type, say which those can be, before anything's
;    decided, so the places and times are in the choices and only two
;    rules are left:
;
;    - a predecessor is taken once (two legs can't both follow one);
;    - an aircraft's minutes, added up along its line, stay within its
;      own.
;
;    A node is an aircraft's start or a leg, and each is an actor, once
;    something sends to it. Its state is (dom pred tail mins next): the
;    predecessors it could still have, the one it has (or -1), its
;    aircraft and its line's minutes so far (once its line reaches back
;    to a start), and the node that took it (or -1). Four messages go
;    between them:
;
;        (:assign p)    you follow p         from the search, or itself
;        (:take j)      j follows you        to a predecessor
;        (:drop p)      you can't follow p   to the others that could have
;        (:line a m)    your line is a's,    down a line, as it's learnt
;                       m minutes so far
;
;    and a node left with one predecessor takes it, which drops it for
;    others, and so on: that's the propagation, and nothing runs it but
;    the mailboxes. Where the simulation knows the day so far, the mold
;    knows what a choice does to the rest of it. A node tells the search
;    of a conflict, (:conflict k), and nothing else of what the rules do.
;
;    What each node does with a message is one function, node-step, of
;    its state and the message, giving its new state and what to send.
;    So the same rules run two ways: as actors (node), and, with
;    --values, as a loop over a tuple of states with a list of messages
;    to work through (v-run).
;
; 3. The search (search, try, flown). It ticks the simulation: the next
;    leg to leave is asked what it could still follow. If the mold has
;    left it one, there's nothing to choose, and the simulation flies
;    it. If more, each is tried: the mold is told and left to settle,
;    and at a conflict the search turns back; else the simulation flies
;    the leg, and the search goes on from there. The simulation and the
;    mold agree on who can fly a leg, the one from where the aircraft
;    are and the other from what's left of the choices, unless a rule is
;    only the simulation's (--check minutes): then the mold lets through
;    what the simulation stops, later. The day flown to its end is an
;    assignment. The search is the same for both ways of keeping the
;    mold, and so are its decisions.
;
; - Quiet: on the virtual clock an island's time moves only when nothing
;   on it can run, so a timer a millisecond off rings exactly when the
;   mold has settled. (Hence SLIGHT_CLOCK=virtual.) --settle system asks
;   the :system device instead: every node waiting with nothing in its
;   mailbox. That works on the real clock too, and costs a message for
;   each process on the island each time it's asked.
; - Turning back: each node keeps the states it had before each level of
;   the search changed it, and (:undo level) puts it back; it tells the
;   search, (:changed k), the first time a level changes it, so only
;   those are told. Nothing's copied: the states are values. With
;   --values there's nothing to undo, the old tuple being still there.
;   The simulation is a value either way, the search's own, so turning
;   back is having kept the airline as it was.
; - Splitting (--split d): the first d choices aren't tried in turn but
;   each given to a process of its own (branch). A search has a range of
;   the islands, all of them at first, and shares it out evenly among
;   the branches it starts, each running on the first island of its
;   share, so the branches of branches spread over every island.
;   The parent asks its nodes for their states, and that tuple, the mold
;   as a value, is what's copied, with the airline; the child grows
;   nodes of its own from it as it touches them, and never turns back
;   past where it began. A node is named by its number, never its pid,
;   so a copy needs no rewiring: a node asks the search whose it is for
;   a pid, once.
; - The bound (--best): the search wants only the cheapest, so it leaves
;   a branch that can't come to less than the best known. What a branch
;   must come to at least (lower): what the legs flown cost, and the
;   minutes of the rest flown by the cheapest aircraft with minutes
;   left, a minute at a time, as if a leg could be shared out; no real
;   assignment is cheaper. It tries the cheapest predecessor first, so a
;   good one is known early. A process (keeper) holds the best any
;   search has found: each tells it, and asks it when it starts and
;   after each thousand decisions, since searches on other islands find
;   things too. The best is the same however it's found; the decisions
;   it takes aren't, with more than one search.
; - The first (--first): the search stops at the first day that flies,
;   which is all a day too big to count can be asked for, and all there
;   is to ask when a minute costs the same whoever flies it. The
;   simulation then flies that day again, alone, as it flies a plan. One
;   search: --split is left aside.
;
; What it found is in docs/PLAN.md, "A mold of constraints".

(@include :fs)
(@include "mold-ssim.slight")

; --- the day ------------------------------------------------------------------

(defun or-0 (v) (if (int? v) v 0))

; More minutes than a day has: no limit.
(defun forever () 100000)

(defun reading (f records)
    (match (read f)
        ((:sexp _ r) (reading f (cons r records)))
        ((:eof _)    (disconnect f) (reverse records))))

(defun read-records (path)
    (match (open :fs/read path)
        ((:ok f)         (send f (list :read :sexp)) (reading f ()))
        ((:error reason) (raise (list :no-day path reason)))))

; A .sexp day is all of one type, which it doesn't say.
(defun typed (r)
    (match r
        ((:turn m)                         (list :turn "" m))
        ((:aircraft tail start limit rate) (list :aircraft tail "" start limit rate))
        ((:leg name from to dep arr)       (list :leg name from to dep arr ""))
        (_                                 r)))

; The day's records: turns (:turn type minutes), aircraft (:aircraft
; tail type start limit rate), legs (:leg flight from to dep arr type),
; and, if there's a plan, (:flown flight tail).
(defun read-day (path slack)
    (if (str/ends-with? path ".sexp")
        (map typed (read-records path))
        (match (slurp path)
            ((:ok lines)     (ssim-day lines slack))
            ((:error reason) (raise (list :no-day path reason))))))

(defun turn?     (r) (match r ((:turn _ _)           #true) (_ #false)))
(defun aircraft? (r) (match r ((:aircraft _ _ _ _ _) #true) (_ #false)))
(defun leg?      (r) (match r ((:leg _ _ _ _ _ _)    #true) (_ #false)))
(defun flown?    (r) (match r ((:flown _ _)          #true) (_ #false)))
(defun leaves    (l) (match l ((:leg _ _ _ dep _ _)   dep)))
(defun block     (l) (match l ((:leg _ _ _ dep arr _) (- arr dep))))
(defun limit-of  (p) (match p ((:aircraft _ _ _ limit _) limit)))
(defun rate-of   (p) (match p ((:aircraft _ _ _ _ rate)  rate)))

(defun number (from xs) (zip (range from (+ from (length xs))) xs))

; The nodes a leg could follow: the starts of the aircraft of its type
; that are where it leaves from and could fly it at all, and the legs of
; its type that land there a turn or more before it leaves.
(defun before (turns fleet legs leg limits)
    (match leg
        ((:leg _ from _ dep arr type)
            (let turn (lookup type turns))
            (append
                (map car (filter (lambda (p) (match p ((a (:aircraft _ mine start _ _))
                                                 (and (eq? start from)
                                                      (and (eq? mine type) (<= (- arr dep) (tuple/get limits a)))))))
                                 fleet))
                (map car (filter (lambda (l) (match l ((_ (:leg _ _ to _ landed mine))
                                                 (and (eq? to from)
                                                      (and (eq? mine type) (<= (+ landed turn) dep))))))
                                 legs))))))

; For each node, the legs that could follow it, each (node minutes), in
; the order they leave: could has, for each leg, (node before minutes).
(defun followers (could size)
    (fold/l (tuple/make size ())
            (lambda (after c)
                (match c
                    ((j dom d)
                        (fold/l after (lambda (t p) (tuple/set t p (cons (list j d) (tuple/get t p)))) dom))))
            (reverse could)))

; The day as the program has it, #(planes legs statics rates initial
; cheapest minutes flights fleet turns plan): how many aircraft and
; legs; for each node (the aircraft's starts, then the legs in the order
; they leave) what never changes, (minutes after limits), after being
; the legs that could follow it, each (node minutes), and limits the
; aircraft's minutes; what a minute of each aircraft costs; each node's
; state before anything's decided; the aircraft, cheapest first, each
; (aircraft rate limit); the minutes of all the legs together; the
; legs' records, in the order they leave, and the aircraft's; each
; type's turn; and for each leg the aircraft the plan gives it, or ()
; without a plan. known is whether the mold knows the aircraft's
; minutes: if not, its limits are forever, and only the simulation's are
; the day's.
(defun day (records known)
    (let turns (map cdr (filter turn? records)))
    (let fleet (number 0 (filter aircraft? records)))
    (let m (length fleet))
    (let legs (number m (sort-by leaves (filter leg? records))))
    (let limits (list->tuple (map (lambda (p) (if known (limit-of (cadr p)) (forever))) fleet)))
    (let could (map (lambda (l) (list (car l) (before turns fleet legs (cadr l) limits) (block (cadr l)))) legs))
    (let after (followers could (+ m (length legs))))
    (let flown (map cdr (filter flown? records)))
    (let tails (map (lambda (p) (match p ((a (:aircraft tail _ _ _ _)) (list tail a)))) fleet))
    (tuple m (length legs)
        (list->tuple (append
            (map (lambda (p) (list 0 (tuple/get after (car p)) limits)) fleet)
            (map (lambda (c) (list (caddr c) (tuple/get after (car c)) limits)) could)))
        (list->tuple (map (lambda (p) (rate-of (cadr p))) fleet))
        (list->tuple (append
            (map (lambda (p) (list () (car p) (car p) 0 -1)) fleet)
            (map (lambda (c) (list (cadr c) -1 -1 0 -1)) could)))
        (sort-by cadr (map (lambda (p) (list (car p) (rate-of (cadr p)) (limit-of (cadr p)))) fleet))
        (sum (map caddr could))
        (list->tuple (map cadr legs))
        (list->tuple (map cadr fleet))
        turns
        (if (nil? flown)
            ()
            (list->tuple (map (lambda (l) (lookup (lookup (flight (cadr l)) flown) tails)) legs)))))

(defun planes   (inst)   (tuple/get inst 0))
(defun legs     (inst)   (tuple/get inst 1))
(defun static   (inst k) (tuple/get (tuple/get inst 2) k))
(defun rate     (inst a) (tuple/get (tuple/get inst 3) a))
(defun initial  (inst)   (tuple/get inst 4))
(defun cheapest (inst)   (tuple/get inst 5))
(defun minutes  (inst)   (tuple/get inst 6))
(defun plan     (inst)   (tuple/get inst 10))

; --- the simulation -----------------------------------------------------------

; The airline as the day goes, (j cost left fleet tails): the leg that
; leaves next; what the legs flown cost, and the minutes of those that
; aren't; each aircraft, (where landed minutes legs last), where it is,
; the minute it landed (-1 before it flies), the minutes and legs it has
; flown, and the node it flew last, its own start at first; and each
; node's aircraft, a leg's -1 till it's flown.
(defun dawn (inst)
    (list 0 0 (minutes inst)
          (list->tuple (map (lambda (ap) (match ap ((a (:aircraft _ _ start _ _)) (list start -1 0 0 a))))
                            (number 0 (tuple->list (tuple/get inst 8)))))
          (list->tuple (map caddr (tuple->list (initial inst))))))

; A tick: the next leg flown by aircraft a, after node p (or, with -1,
; after whatever it flew last). (:ok airline), or (:stops j why), the
; leg it stops at.
(defun fly (inst air a p)
    (match air
        ((j cost left fleet tails)
            (if (== a -1)
                (list :stops j :no-aircraft)
                (fly-on inst air a p (tuple/get (tuple/get inst 7) j)
                        (tuple/get (tuple/get inst 8) a) (tuple/get fleet a))))))

(defun fly-on (inst air a p leg plane now)
    (match air ((j cost left fleet tails)
        (match leg ((:leg _ from to dep arr type)
            (match plane ((:aircraft _ mine _ limit per)
                (match now ((where landed flew cycles last)
                    (let d (- arr dep))
                    (cond
                        ((ne? mine type)                   (list :stops j :wrong-type))
                        ((ne? where from)                  (list :stops j :not-there))
                        ((and (!= p -1) (!= last p))       (list :stops j :flown-on))
                        ((and (!= landed -1) (> (+ landed (lookup type (tuple/get inst 9))) dep))
                                                           (list :stops j :no-turn))
                        ((> (+ flew d) limit)              (list :stops j :minutes))
                        (#true
                            (let k (+ (planes inst) j))
                            (list :ok (list (+ j 1) (+ cost (* d per)) (- left d)
                                            (tuple/set fleet a (list to arr (+ flew d) (+ cycles 1) k))
                                            (tuple/set tails k a))))))))))))))

; The whole day flown, each leg by the aircraft by gives it.
(defun fly-all (inst air by)
    (if (== (car air) (legs inst))
        (list :ok air)
        (match (fly inst air (tuple/get by (car air)) -1)
            ((:ok air2) (fly-all inst air2 by))
            (stops      stops))))

; --- a node's rules -----------------------------------------------------------

; What node k does with a message: (state sends), its new state (the old
; one itself if nothing changed) and what it sends, each (to message), to
; being a node, or -1 for the search.
(defun node-step (k static st msg)
    (match msg
        ((:assign p) (step-assign k st p))
        ((:drop p)   (step-drop k st p))
        ((:take j)   (step-take k static st j))
        ((:line a m) (step-line k static st a m))))

(defun conflict (k st) (list st (list (list -1 (list :conflict k)))))

(defun step-assign (k st p)
    (match st
        ((dom pred tail mins next)
            (cond
                ((== pred p)           (list st ()))
                ((!= pred -1)          (conflict k st))
                ((not (member? p dom)) (conflict k st))
                (#true
                    (list (list (list p) p tail mins next)
                          (list (list p (list :take k)))))))))

; Left with one it could follow, a node follows it.
(defun step-drop (k st p)
    (match st
        ((dom pred tail mins next)
            (cond
                ((not (member? p dom)) (list st ()))
                ((== pred p)           (conflict k st))
                (#true
                    (let left (remove (lambda (q) (== q p)) dom))
                    (match left
                        (()  (conflict k st))
                        ((q) (step-assign k (list left pred tail mins next) q))
                        (_   (list (list left pred tail mins next) ()))))))))

; Taken, a node is no one else's to follow, and passes on its line if it
; knows it.
(defun step-take (k static st j)
    (match st
        ((dom pred tail mins next)
            (cond
                ((== next j)  (list st ()))
                ((!= next -1) (conflict k st))
                (#true
                    (let drops (map (lambda (s) (list (car s) (list :drop k)))
                                    (filter (lambda (s) (!= (car s) j)) (cadr static))))
                    (list (list dom pred tail mins j)
                          (if (== tail -1) drops (cons (list j (list :line tail mins)) drops))))))))

; Its line learnt, a node passes it on, or, with no one after it yet,
; drops itself for the legs that would take the aircraft past its minutes.
(defun step-line (k static st a m)
    (match st
        ((dom pred _ _ next)
            (match static
                ((flies after limits)
                    (let mine (+ m flies))
                    (let limit (tuple/get limits a))
                    (if (> mine limit)
                        (conflict k st)
                        (list (list dom pred a mine next)
                              (if (!= next -1)
                                  (list (list next (list :line a mine)))
                                  (map (lambda (s) (list (car s) (list :drop k)))
                                       (filter (lambda (s) (> (+ mine (cadr s)) limit)) after))))))))))

; What the search keeps of what the nodes tell it, (bad changed):
; whether any node found a conflict; and the nodes, actors only, whose
; states this level changed, to put back.
(defun note (acc msg)
    (match acc
        ((bad changed)
            (match msg
                ((:conflict _) (list #true changed))
                ((:changed k)  (list bad (cons k changed)))))))

; --- the mold as a value ------------------------------------------------------

; The messages worked through, newest first, till there are none or a
; node finds a conflict: (states acc).
(defun v-run (inst states queue acc)
    (match queue
        (() (list states acc))
        (((to msg) & rest)
            (if (== to -1)
                (list states (note acc msg))
                (match (node-step to (static inst to) (tuple/get states to) msg)
                    ((st sends)
                        (v-run inst
                               (if (eq? st (tuple/get states to)) states (tuple/set states to st))
                               (append sends rest)
                               acc)))))))

; --- the mold as actors -------------------------------------------------------

; A node: its number, what never changes for it, the search it's part
; of, its state, the states it had before each level changed it, newest
; first, each (level state), and the pids of the nodes it has sent to.
; The first time a level changes it, it tells the search, which is how
; the search knows whom to tell to put it back.
(defun node (k static search st undo known)
    (recv
        ((:msg level m)
            (match (node-step k static st m)
                ((st2 sends)
                    (if (or (eq? st2 st) (and (cons? undo) (>= (caar undo) level)))
                        (node k static search st2 undo (deliver search level sends known))
                        (do (send search (list :changed k))
                            (node k static search st2 (cons (list level st) undo)
                                  (deliver search level sends known)))))))
        ((:undo level)
            (match (unwind undo level st)
                ((st2 undo2) (node k static search st2 undo2 known))))
        ((:state to)
            (reply to st)
            (node k static search st undo known))))

(defun unwind (undo level st)
    (match undo
        (((l was) & rest) (if (>= l level) (unwind rest level was) (list st undo)))
        (()               (list st undo))))

; Sends each, asking the search for the pid of a node not sent to before
; (which grows it, if it wasn't there): the pids known after.
(defun deliver (search level sends known)
    (match sends
        (() known)
        (((to msg) & rest)
            (if (== to -1)
                (do (send search msg)
                    (deliver search level rest known))
                (match (lookup to known)
                    (:not-found
                        (let pid (ask search (list :who to)))
                        (send pid (list :msg level msg))
                        (deliver search level rest (cons (list to pid) known)))
                    (pid
                        (send pid (list :msg level msg))
                        (deliver search level rest known)))))))

; The search's side of a mold of actors, #(pids mold sys): the pid of
; each node that's grown, or (); the state each of the others would
; start from; and the :system device, if that's how it's asked whether
; the mold is quiet.
(defun grow (inst world k)
    (match world
        (#(pids mold sys)
            (if (pid? (tuple/get pids k))
                world
                (tuple (tuple/set pids k (fork node k (static inst k) $$ (tuple/get mold k) () ()))
                       mold sys)))))

(defun pid-of (world k) (tuple/get (tuple/get world 0) k))
(defun grown  (world)   (filter pid? (tuple->list (tuple/get world 0))))

; Waits till the mold is quiet, answering the nodes that ask for a pid
; and keeping what they tell: (world acc).
(defun settle (inst world acc)
    (recv
        ((:who k to)
            (let w (grow inst world k))
            (reply to (pid-of w k))
            (settle inst w acc))
        (:settled (list world acc))
        (msg      (settle inst world (note acc msg)))))

; The same by asking :system: what's waiting for the search is taken, up
; to a mark it sends itself; then the island's processes are asked for,
; and the mold is quiet if the search has nothing waiting and each of its
; nodes waits with nothing either. If not, the others get a turn first.
(defun settle/system (inst world acc)
    (send $$ :mark)
    (match (drain inst world acc)
        ((w a)
            (let sys (tuple/get w 2))
            (send sys (list :processes (island)))
            (if (quiet? sys $$ #true)
                (list w a)
                (yield (settle/system inst w a))))))

(defun drain (inst world acc)
    (recv
        ((:who k to)
            (let w (grow inst world k))
            (reply to (pid-of w k))
            (drain inst w acc))
        (:mark (list world acc))
        (msg   (drain inst world (note acc msg)))))

(defun quiet? (sys me so-far)
    (match (read sys)
        ((:end _) so-far)
        ((:process _ info)
            (quiet? sys me
                (and so-far
                     (cond
                         ((eq? (lookup :pid info) me)    (== (lookup :mail info) 0))
                         ((eq? (lookup :parent info) me) (and (eq? (lookup :state info) :recv)
                                                              (== (lookup :mail info) 0)))
                         (#true                          #true)))))))

; --- the search ---------------------------------------------------------------

; What's the same whichever way the mold is kept: cx is #(inst actors
; split system from to keeper first), the day, whether the mold is
; actors, how many choices deep the search splits, whether :system says
; when it's quiet, the islands that are this search's to share out, from
; one up to but not including another, in 4096ths of an island, the
; process that keeps the best cost found, or () when every assignment is
; wanted, and whether the first day that flies is all that is. A world
; is a mold: a tuple of states, or the search's side of the actors.

(defun fresh (cx mold)
    (if (tuple/get cx 1)
        (tuple (tuple/make (tuple/len mold) ()) mold
               (if (tuple/get cx 3) (match (open :system) ((:ok sys) sys)) ()))
        mold))

; Node k told to follow v, and the mold left to settle: (world acc).
(defun decide (cx world k v level)
    (let inst (tuple/get cx 0))
    (cond
        ((not (tuple/get cx 1))
            (v-run inst world (list (list k (list :assign v))) (list #false ())))
        (#true
            (let w (grow inst world k))
            (send (pid-of w k) (list :msg level (list :assign v)))
            (if (tuple/get cx 3)
                (settle/system inst w (list #false ()))
                (do (after 1 $$ :settled)
                    (settle inst w (list #false ())))))))

; The world as it was before a level: the tuple from before it, or the
; actors it changed told to put back what they had.
(defun retract (cx was world level changed)
    (if (tuple/get cx 1)
        (do (map (lambda (k) (send (pid-of world k) (list :undo level))) changed)
            world)
        was))

; Node k's state.
(defun state (cx world k)
    (cond
        ((not (tuple/get cx 1))  (tuple/get world k))
        ((pid? (pid-of world k)) (ask (pid-of world k) (list :state)))
        (#true                   (tuple/get (tuple/get world 1) k))))

; What a leg could follow, in the order to try them: as they come, or,
; when it's the cheapest that's wanted, the cheapest aircraft's first.
(defun choices (cx air dom)
    (if (pid? (tuple/get cx 6))
        (match air
            ((_ _ _ _ tails)
                (sort-by (lambda (p) (rate (tuple/get cx 0) (tuple/get tails p))) dom)))
        dom))

; The mold as a value, to start a branch from: the tuple itself, or each
; grown node asked for its state.
(defun snapshot (cx world)
    (if (tuple/get cx 1)
        (fold/l (tuple/get world 1)
                (lambda (mold k)
                    (if (pid? (pid-of world k))
                        (tuple/set mold k (ask (pid-of world k) (list :state)))
                        mold))
                (range 0 (tuple/len (tuple/get world 1))))
        world))

; A search's nodes ended with it: how many it grew.
(defun finish (cx world)
    (if (tuple/get cx 1)
        (do (map kill (grown world))
            (if (tuple/get cx 3) (disconnect (tuple/get world 2)) ())
            (length (grown world)))
        0))

; A result is (assignments best decisions conflicts bounded stops forks
; nodes found): best the least cost, or -1 with no assignment; bounded
; the branches left because they couldn't beat the best known; stops
; those the simulation stopped; and found, when the first is all that's
; wanted, each node's aircraft in it.
(defun least (a b) (cond ((== a -1) b) ((== b -1) a) (#true (math/min a b))))
(defun add (x y)
    (match x ((c1 b1 d1 x1 l1 s1 f1 n1 t1)
        (match y ((c2 b2 d2 x2 l2 s2 f2 n2 t2)
            (list (+ c1 c2) (least b1 b2) (+ d1 d2) (+ x1 x2) (+ l1 l2) (+ s1 s2) (+ f1 f2) (+ n1 n2)
                  (if (nil? t1) t2 t1)))))))

(defun tally (decisions conflicts bounded stops)
    (list 0 -1 decisions conflicts bounded stops 0 0 ()))

(defun ok (joined) (match joined ((:ok r) r) ((:error reason) (raise reason))))

; --- the bound ----------------------------------------------------------------

; The least a search could still come to: what's flown already, and the
; minutes that aren't, each on the cheapest aircraft with minutes left;
; -1 if the aircraft haven't the minutes between them.
(defun lower (order fleet left cost)
    (cond
        ((<= left 0)  cost)
        ((nil? order) -1)
        (#true
            (match (car order)
                ((a per limit)
                    (let room (math/min left (- limit (caddr (tuple/get fleet a)))))
                    (lower (cdr order) fleet (- left room) (+ cost (* room per))))))))

; Whether to leave a branch: it can't come to less than the best known.
(defun cut? (cx air bound)
    (if (pid? (tuple/get cx 6))
        (match air
            ((_ cost left fleet _)
                (let low (lower (cheapest (tuple/get cx 0)) fleet left cost))
                (or (== low -1) (and (!= bound -1) (>= low bound)))))
        #false))

; The best cost any search has found, or -1.
(defun keeper (best)
    (recv
        ((:found cost) (keeper (least best cost)))
        ((:best to)    (reply to best) (keeper best))))

; The bound for what's tried next: the least of what was known and what
; the last choice came to; and, after a thousand decisions or more with
; other searches about, of what the keeper has heard since.
(defun heard (cx bound r)
    (let known (least bound (cadr r)))
    (if (and (pid? (tuple/get cx 6)) (and (> (tuple/get cx 2) 0) (>= (caddr r) 1000)))
        (least known (ask (tuple/get cx 6) (list :best)))
        known))

; --- ticking, and going on, stopping or branching ----------------------------

; Every assignment from a settled world and the airline so far, or every
; one that beats the bound, or the first: (world result).
(defun search (cx world air bound depth)
    (let inst (tuple/get cx 0))
    (match air
        ((j cost _ _ tails)
            (cond
                ((== j (legs inst))
                    (when (pid? (tuple/get cx 6))
                        (send (tuple/get cx 6) (list :found cost)))
                    (list world (list 1 cost 0 0 0 0 0 0 (if (tuple/get cx 7) tails ()))))
                (#true
                    (let k (+ (planes inst) j))
                    (match (state cx world k)
                        ((dom pred _ _ _)
                            (cond
                                ((!= pred -1)
                                    (flown cx world air bound depth pred))
                                ((< depth (tuple/get cx 2))
                                    (let picks (choices cx air dom))
                                    (let mold (snapshot cx world))
                                    (let share (div (- (tuple/get cx 5) (tuple/get cx 4)) (math/max 1 (length picks))))
                                    (let pids (map (lambda (iv)
                                                       (let from (+ (tuple/get cx 4) (* (car iv) share)))
                                                       (fork/on (div from 4096) branch
                                                                (tuple/set (tuple/set cx 4 from) 5 (+ from share))
                                                                mold air bound depth k (cadr iv)))
                                                   (zip (range 0 (length picks)) picks)))
                                    (list world (fold/l (list 0 -1 0 0 0 0 (length picks) 0 ()) add
                                                        (map ok (map join pids)))))
                                (#true
                                    (try cx world air bound depth k (choices cx air dom) (tally 0 0 0 0)))))))))))

; The tick itself: the next leg flown after node p, by the aircraft
; that flew p, and the search going on from there, unless the simulation
; stops it, or the bound does.
(defun flown (cx world air bound depth p)
    (match air
        ((_ _ _ _ tails)
            (match (fly (tuple/get cx 0) air (tuple/get tails p) p)
                ((:stops _ _) (list world (tally 0 0 0 1)))
                ((:ok air2)   (if (cut? cx air2 bound)
                                  (list world (tally 0 0 1 0))
                                  (search cx world air2 bound depth)))))))

; Node k following each of dom in turn, and all that comes of each.
(defun try (cx world air bound depth k dom sum)
    (match dom
        (() (list world sum))
        ((v & rest)
            (match (decide cx world k v (+ depth 1))
                ((w (bad changed))
                    (match (if bad (list w (tally 0 1 0 0)) (flown cx w air bound (+ depth 1) v))
                        ((w2 r)
                            (let all (add sum (add r (tally 1 0 0 0))))
                            (if (and (tuple/get cx 7) (> (car r) 0))
                                (list w2 all)
                                (try cx (retract cx world w2 (+ depth 1) changed) air (heard cx bound r)
                                     depth k rest all)))))))))

; A process for one choice: a mold of its own, from its parent's as a
; value, and all that comes of node k following v, against the best
; known as it starts.
(defun branch (cx mold air bound depth k v)
    (let known (if (pid? (tuple/get cx 6))
                   (least bound (ask (tuple/get cx 6) (list :best)))
                   bound))
    (match (try cx (fresh cx mold) air known depth k (list v) (tally 0 0 0 0))
        ((w r) (add r (list 0 -1 0 0 0 0 0 (finish cx w) ())))))

; --- the program --------------------------------------------------------------

; What each aircraft did, and what the day came to.
(defun flew (inst air)
    (match air
        ((_ _ left fleet _)
            (map (lambda (pn)
                     (match pn
                         (((:aircraft tail _ start _ _) (where _ flies cycles _))
                             (tty/write tail " " start " to " where ": " cycles " legs, " flies " minutes\n"))))
                 (zip (tuple->list (tuple/get inst 8)) (tuple->list fleet)))
            (str (legs inst) " legs, " (- (minutes inst) left) " minutes"))))

; The simulation alone: the day as its plan has it.
(defun fly-plan (inst stats)
    (if (nil? (plan inst))
        (raise "there's no plan in this day to fly: an SSIM file has one")
        (match (fly-all inst (dawn inst) (plan inst))
            ((:ok air)
                (tty/write "the plan flies: " (flew inst air) "\n"))
            ((:stops j why)
                (tty/write "the plan stops at " (flight (tuple/get (tuple/get inst 7) j)) "\n")
                (when stats (tty/write "    " why "\n"))))))

(defun solve (inst o)
    (match o
        (#(_ actors split system stats best first _ _ _)
            (let cx (tuple inst actors (if first 0 split) system 0 (* (islands) 4096)
                           (if best (fork keeper -1) ()) first))
            (match (search cx (fresh cx (initial inst)) (dawn inst) -1 0)
                ((w (count least-cost decisions conflicts bounded stops forks nodes found))
                    (cond
                        (first
                            (if (nil? found)
                                (tty/write "no day flies\n")
                                (match (fly-all inst (dawn inst)
                                                (tuple/slice found (planes inst) (tuple/len found)))
                                    ((:ok air)   (tty/write "a day that flies: "
                                                            (legs inst) " legs, "
                                                            (- (minutes inst) (caddr air)) " minutes\n"))
                                    ((:stops j why) (raise (list :the-simulation-stops j why))))))
                        (#true
                            (when (not best) (tty/write count " assignments\n"))
                            (tty/write (if (== least-cost -1) "no best" (str "best " least-cost)) "\n")))
                    (when stats
                        (tty/write "decisions " decisions ", conflicts " conflicts
                                   ", bounded " bounded ", stops " stops ", forks " forks
                                   ", nodes " (+ nodes (finish cx w)) "\n"))
                    (when best (kill (tuple/get cx 6)))
                    ())))))

(defun main (o clock)
    (match o
        (#(path actors _ system stats _ _ fly-it slack checked)
            (let inst (day (read-day path slack) (not checked)))
            (tty/write (legs inst) " legs, " (planes inst) " aircraft\n")
            (cond
                (fly-it
                    (fly-plan inst stats))
                ((and actors (and (not system) (ne? clock "virtual")))
                    (raise "the clock says when the mold is quiet: run with SLIGHT_CLOCK=virtual, or --settle system"))
                (#true
                    (solve inst o))))))

(defun options (args o clock)
    (match args
        (()                           (main o clock))
        (("--values" & rest)          (options rest (tuple/set o 1 #false) clock))
        (("--split" n & rest)         (options rest (tuple/set o 2 (or-0 (str->int n))) clock))
        (("--settle" "system" & rest) (options rest (tuple/set o 3 #true) clock))
        (("--settle" "clock" & rest)  (options rest (tuple/set o 3 #false) clock))
        (("--stats" & rest)           (options rest (tuple/set o 4 #true) clock))
        (("--best" & rest)            (options rest (tuple/set o 5 #true) clock))
        (("--first" & rest)           (options rest (tuple/set o 6 #true) clock))
        (("--fly" & rest)             (options rest (tuple/set o 7 #true) clock))
        (("--slack" n & rest)         (options rest (tuple/set o 8 (or-0 (str->int n))) clock))
        (("--check" "minutes" & rest) (options rest (tuple/set o 9 #true) clock))
        ((p & rest)                   (options rest (tuple/set o 0 p) clock))))

(options @ARGV (tuple "examples/mold-day.sexp" #true 0 #false #false #false #false #false -1 #false)
         (lookup "SLIGHT_CLOCK" %ENV))
